@{
    Layout = "_Layout";
}
@*
    Renders through ISCC.Shared.Web/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml.

    It was "Layout = null" while the login page was standalone and carried its own inline
    CSS, which bypassed the shared shell entirely. That hid the fact that no wwwroot existed
    anywhere in the solution and that the layout — where the signed-in user's name and
    outlet appear — had never been exercised by a real page.

    MVC resolves _Layout by convention across application parts, so this picks up the shared
    one rather than a per-host copy.
*@